//? Title: Sparse Bayesian regression: actual precision updates and matched predictive variance
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Fit a Gaussian-kernel regression model with independent prior precisions that
can suppress individual basis functions. Actual posterior and hyperparameter
histories precede the original 41-point noiseless sine fit and 201-point
prediction grid.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For bias-first design Phi and diagonal prior precision A,
$$ \Sigma=(A+\beta\Phi^T\Phi)^{-1},\qquad\mu=\beta\Sigma\Phi^Tt. $$
\alttext(The posterior covariance is the inverse prior plus likelihood precision; the posterior mean solves the same precision system.)
Re-estimate gamma_j=1-alpha_j*Sigma_jj, alpha_j=gamma_j/mu_j^2 and beta=(n-sum
gamma_j)/(SSE+1e-12), with the documented finite fallback rules. A positive
finite threshold selects active nonbias bases; the bias remains. Crucially the
final active model is refitted using the final reported alpha and beta, so mean
and covariance match. Predictive variance is phi^T*Sigma*phi+1/beta. This fixes
the historical stale-weight/pruning mismatch. Fixed-point updates have no global
evidence optimum guarantee; no monotone objective is asserted. Cholesky uses
widened arithmetic and may reject numerically non-SPD systems.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rvm_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::RVMOptions o;
    o.max_iterations = 0;
    auto r = a::rvm_train_trace({{0}, {1}}, {0, 1}, o);
    auto p = a::rvm_predictive(r, {.5});
    std::print("Actual initial-prior posterior means `{}`; solves {}; mean {}, latent variance {}, noise " "variance {}.\n",
               r.model.weights, r.posterior_solves, p.mean, p.latent_variance,
               p.noise_variance);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Bias plus two Gaussian bases");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual posterior solves {}",
                                     r.posterior_solves));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual midpoint mean {:.4f}", p.mean));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/rvm_tiny.svg");
}
```
